{"name":"Masala Chai","hex":"#eeccaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"masala chai","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A South Asian beverage of black tea brewed in milk and water and then sweetened with sugar, with the addition of aromatic herbs and spices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masala_chai"}],"entries":[{"title":"Masala chai","blocks":[{"text":"Masala chai is a popular beverage originating from India. It is made by adding aromatic herbs and spices to chai, which is made from brewing black tea in milk and water, and sweetening with sugar, often using aeration techniques only performed by masters or \"tevanas\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Chai_In_Sakora.jpg/330px-Chai_In_Sakora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_chai","wikidata":"Q877661"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg/500px-Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg/500px-Chai-Kwon-Do.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typical spices used for masala chai","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChai-Kwon-Do.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Teamaking.JPG/500px-Teamaking.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Teamaking.JPG/500px-Teamaking.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy in Mysore preparing masala chai: As it is prepared by decoction, preparation usually includes straining tea from the solids.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeamaking.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik